## Assembly

[28] build/assemble.sh builds output/<job>/final from the two fragments. It compiles in
     PLAYGROUND/build/compile, not in OUTPUT, so no .aux/.log/.fls ever lands in the
     deliverable (R4), and copies back only main.tex, preamble.tex, p1.tex, p2.tex,
     main.pdf and fig_p2_layer.pdf.
[29] Three build decisions, each after a failed or noisy compile:
     - `\usepackage[T1]{fontenc}` alone killed the compile: this TinyTeX has no cm-super
       (`Font ecbx1000 at 600 not found`) and tlmgr cannot install into a read-only
       ~/.TinyTeX. Added `\usepackage{lmodern}`, which ships T1 Latin Modern and is
       present. Recorded here as the substitution env.md asks for.
     - hyperref loaded before the workers' `float` gave "destination with the same
       identifier (name{table.N}) has been already used" for every [H] float. Moving
       hyperref to the end of the merged preamble clears all of them.
     - `\setcounter{secnumdepth}{0}`: the sections are already named Q1/Q2/Q3, so LaTeX
       numbering them 1/2/3 on top of that read badly.
[30] The cover page is reproduced in main.tex because the assignment requires it ("as a
     PDF or Word file including the cover page"). Its three fields are left blank, exactly
     as the handout's form has them -- I do not know the student's name or the assignment
     date, and inventing either would be worse than leaving the form to be filled in.
[31] On the handout's "submit only your implemented code file": this pipeline's deliverable
