## Submission round 1 -> FAIL, four defects, all fixed

[34] 01:24 master validator round 1 -> FAIL. It re-ran cells 14, 18, 19 and 22 itself,
     reproduced Table 1's bolded row exactly (val 0.5160 / test 0.5496 / epoch 30), every
     pair count in Tables 2 and 3, every params figure and every Table 4 mean, and read
     past both GraphGPS quotations in the paper. It found no wrong answer, no missing
     sub-part and no compile problem. Four defects, all located precisely:
     - [D1.1] major: p2's \lstdefinestyle{p2python} lacked `columns=fullflexible` (and
       `breakindent`), so the Q3 listing typeset as `class HybridGTLayer ( nn . Module ) :`
       while Q1/Q2 under p1py typeset cleanly -- the same document setting code two ways,
       in an assignment whose deliverable is the code.
     - [D1.2] minor: "moves it by 0.0119, inside the $\pm$0.0100 seed half-range" -- 0.0119
       is outside a half-range of 0.0100.
     - [D1.3] minor: Table 1 and Table 4 report the same two baselines (0.7013/0.4957 and
       0.693/0.495) with nothing saying they are separate measurements.
     - [D1.4] minor: "the constant eigenvector $D^{1/2}\mathbf{1}$" -- that vector is
       constant only on a regular graph, and ZINC molecules are not.
[35] I fixed all four myself in the workers' answer.tex rather than respawning: each is a
     one-line edit the validator specified exactly, and respawning a passed worker to
     reword a clause risks churning answers that have already been reproduced. Backups of
     both fragments are in build/p1_answer.bak and build/p2_answer.bak.
     - D1.1: added `breakindent=2em, columns=fullflexible` to p2python.
     - D1.2: "inside the 0.0200 seed spread of the full-attention row of Table 2" -- the
       spread, which 0.0119 really is inside, so the conclusion stands on a true premise.
     - D1.3: one clause in Table 4's caption saying the baselines were measured again for
       that table rather than copied, and that the gaps (0.0083 and 0.0007) are inside the
       0.009 run-to-run noise the same paragraph already quotes. I checked both arithmetic
       claims before writing them.
     - D1.4: "constant" -> "trivial", which is what the rest of the fragment already calls it.
[36] Rebuilt: 9 pages, no undefined references, no duplicate destinations, the same single
     2.56pt overfull box. Both worker dirs and the final dir lint clean.
[37] Verified the D1.1 fix rather than assuming it: the Q3 listing lifted out of the PDF
